                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9e66dd26-a936-3939-9218-b5c64e365b69",
                        "entry_id": "1e1e66de-0846-3492-a456-b0a64328f25e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Understanding law; skilled in jurisprudence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d21ea73f-c8a1-4e71-8069-152478a376ef",
                                "sense_id": "9e66dd26-a936-3939-9218-b5c64e365b69",
                                "text": "For if belligerent rights were worthy to be gravely discussed by conferences and commissions of very jurisprudent gentlemen, why shall not expectorant rights — never until now discussed or settled, but existing only in the great common or unwritten law of usage—be once for all clearly confirmed, settled, and defined?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cadc1562-ecca-4f6e-bb49-9452f8e86eb5",
                                "sense_id": "9e66dd26-a936-3939-9218-b5c64e365b69",
                                "text": "'Adieu!' he says, 'I am going to my tutor's lectures on one Puffendorf, a very jurisprudent author as you shall read on a summer's day.'"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "59941511-8337-3d49-9953-9d0e350e86ff",
                        "entry_id": "1e1e66de-0846-3492-a456-b0a64328f25e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pertaining to jurisprudence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "844df6fc-10db-436c-b95b-04c973b22a44",
                                "sense_id": "59941511-8337-3d49-9953-9d0e350e86ff",
                                "text": "“And you can't be drinking alcohol on the community stairs, either,” he added, very jurisprudent."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "082c7cb5-b025-49a0-864d-d8772c7323a7",
                                "sense_id": "59941511-8337-3d49-9953-9d0e350e86ff",
                                "text": "By this, I wanted to point out how subtle and conscientious our judgment of jurisprudent ideas should be, and what kind of historic approach we have to cherish towards them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1a4a05e4-5430-4652-a1cd-da680ebd1094",
                                "sense_id": "59941511-8337-3d49-9953-9d0e350e86ff",
                                "text": "The jurisprudent psychology analysis is designed to ensure that the results of clinical and forensic interventions for each individual comport with the law's emphasis on principles of justice and fairness."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "536a94df-cf96-42da-8d0c-9a5728a44001",
                                "sense_id": "59941511-8337-3d49-9953-9d0e350e86ff",
                                "text": "It is much more prudent and therefore also much more jurisprudent to endeavour to understand what really happens in law and legal theory."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
